{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"inherited-evadable-dachshund","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe accepted clarity analysis on ticket e759-c562-e233-4108 identified two structurally unambiguous plan defects that the current length-and-heading heuristic does not reject: empty parsed Acceptance Criteria items and unresolved sentinel assignments in active execution sections. Standalone clarity and deterministic P1 must enforce the same floor without changing ticket-type exemptions or the legacy compatibility score.\n\n## Approach\n- Add one pure shared plan-structure helper that parses standard Acceptance Criteria checkbox items with wrapped continuations and detects unresolved sentinel assignments only in exact active execution sections.\n- Wire the helper into standalone `clarity_check_compute` and plan-review `p1_readiness_shape`, preserving the existing clarity score as compatibility coverage.\n- Add focused behavior tests before implementation, including historical negative controls and agreement between the two gate surfaces.\n\n## Scope\n- Add `src/rebar/_plan_clarity.py` for the shared structural parser and hard-floor result.\n- Update `src/rebar/_engine_support/gates.py` to apply the result to standalone clarity.\n- Update `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py` to emit blocking P1 findings for the same defects.\n- Add `tests/unit/test_clarity_floor.py` for focused unit and cross-surface regression coverage.\n\n## Testing\n- Run the focused clarity-floor tests during the red-green cycle.\n- Run the repository lint, typecheck, and full test gates after the focused suite is green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A standard Acceptance Criteria checkbox whose fully joined body is whitespace-empty fails standalone clarity.\n- [ ] A checkbox with a blank first line and a nonblank wrapped continuation passes the nonempty-item rule.\n- [ ] Sentinel-as-value forms in exact Approach, Scope, Testing, or Acceptance Criteria sections fail standalone clarity.\n- [ ] Fenced code, inline code, ordinary prose mentions, and same-line removal or negation assertions do not trigger the sentinel rule.\n- [ ] Plan-review P1 blocks on each new defect and passes the historical `NO stale TODO` negative control.\n- [ ] Focused tests, lint, typecheck, and the full repository test suite pass.","id":"9385-4ba8-ec93-44c3","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["clarity","plan-review","gates"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Enforce deterministic clarity floors for executable plans"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785191917835107001,"uuid":"5657ae45-ff2e-4412-ae1a-86e299cbc73a"}